'''Communication physics''' is one of the applied branches of [[physics]].  It deals with various kinds of [[communication systems]].<ref name=":0">{{Citation |last=Sostrin |first=Jesse |chapter=Communication Physics: What Holds Patterns Together |date=2013 |chapter-url=https://doi.org/10.1057/9781137332769_8 |title=Re-Making Communication at Work |pages=81–87 |editor-last=Sostrin |editor-first=Jesse |access-date=2023-03-26 |place=New York |publisher=Palgrave Macmillan US |language=en |doi=10.1057/9781137332769_8 |isbn=978-1-137-33276-9|chapter-url-access=subscription }}</ref> These can range from basic ideas such as [[mobile phone communication]] to quantum communication via quantum entanglement.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Smart |first=Scott E. |last2=Hu |first2=Zixuan |last3=Kais |first3=Sabre |last4=Mazziotti |first4=David A. |date=2022-01-25 |title=Relaxation of stationary states on a quantum computer yields a unique spectroscopic fingerprint of the computer's noise |url=https://www.nature.com/articles/s42005-022-00803-8 |journal=Communications Physics |language=en |volume=5 |issue=1 |pages=1–7 |doi=10.1038/s42005-022-00803-8  |doi-access=free|issn=2399-3650|arxiv=2104.14552 }}</ref> [[Communications Physics|Communication physics]] is also a journal edition created in 2018 published by Nature Research that aims to publish research that involves a different way of thinking in the research field.<ref>{{Cite journal |date=2018-02-22 |title=Introducing Communications Physics |url=https://www.nature.com/articles/s42005-018-0008-5 |journal=Communications Physics |language=en |volume=1 |issue=1 |pages=1–2 |doi=10.1038/s42005-018-0008-5 |issn=2399-3650|doi-access=free }}</ref>

