'''''Astronomy Now''''' is a monthly British [[magazine]] on [[astronomy]] and space. In an article published by the [[Royal Astronomical Society]] in 2012, ''Astronomy Now'' was characterized as the "principal amateur astronomy magazine in Britain" with a reputed circulation of 24,000.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ras.org.uk/education-and-careers/208-miscellaneous/915-british-astronomy-amateur-and-educational-astronomy-in-britain |title=British Astronomy – Amateur and Educational Astronomy in Britain |publisher=[[Royal Astronomical Society]] |access-date=November 23, 2012}}</ref>

The magazine features articles ranging from how to observe the night sky to the latest discoveries in the Solar System and in deep space. The first issue of ''Astronomy Now'' was published in April 1987 by Intra Press, initially as a quarterly publication, but it soon became monthly. It is published by Pole Star Publications Ltd.{{citation needed|date=November 2012}}
